Modifications
-------------

The files are vendored verbatim without modification. No patches have
been applied.

Why vendored?
-------------

The `third_party/iree_compat/` directory exists because the IREE binary
distributions we encountered are incomplete: they ship the runtime static
libraries (`libiree_runtime_*.a`) but omit several public headers (e.g.,
`iree/base/allocator.h`, `iree/base/status.h`). Vendoring these 363
headers from the authentic upstream source at tag `iree-3.11.0` is the
only way to link against the runtime libraries without falling back to a
header-incomplete dist.

When upstream IREE binary distributions ship complete headers, this
vendoring layer can be removed.

